            "title_type": "TV Series",
            "description": "Conversations with Friends (2022), directed by Lenny Abrahamson and Leanne Welham, is a drama-romance adaptation of Sally Rooney’s novel that follows Frances (Alison Oliver), her ex-girlfriend Bobbi (Sasha Lane), and a complicated relationship they form with a married couple, Nick (Joe Alwyn) and Melissa (Jemima Kirke). The series is a character-led exploration of desire and friendship: through intimate conversations, artistic performance, and shifting power dynamics it traces how attraction, jealousy, and vulnerability reshape the characters’ identities and connections. Blending dramatic realism with psychological depth, the show foregrounds themes of love, friendship, intellectual entanglement, and emotional exposure, and maintains a quietly intense, lyrical, and atmospheric tone throughout.",
            "finale_year": 2022,
            "wikidata_id": "q107980534",
            "plot_summary": "A young university student and aspiring poet becomes entangled in a shifting network of desire and obligation when she and her former girlfriend meet and form a complicated relationship with a charismatic, older married man and his partner. The story traces the slow, intimate unspooling of friendships and affairs: flirtations that begin as intellectual stimulation and performance, then deepen into jealousy, secrecy, and moral uncertainty. Interpersonal power balances—age, social status, charisma—are tested as characters use conversation, sex, and art to probe one another’s weaknesses and longings. The narrative focuses on interior life and small gestures, showing how private conversations accumulate into life-changing choices and leave each person more exposed and uncertain about who they are and what they want.",
